  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2009-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Any four consecutive powers of \\(3\\) sum to a multiple of \\(3^0+3^1+3^2+3^3=40,\\) which is divisible by \\(8.\\)\n\nThe terms from \\(3^2\\) to \\(3^{2009}\\) split into such blocks and contribute remainder \\(0.\\) What remains is \\(3^0+3^1=4.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(3^0+3^1+3^2+3^3=40\\) is a multiple of \\(8\\)",
        "Group the \\(2010\\) terms into blocks of four and handle the leftover"
      ],
